      "summaries": {
        "en": "PhotoGIMP is a patch that adapts GIMP 3+ to feel like Adobe Photoshop, reducing the learning curve for Photoshop users migrating to open-source tools. It rearranges menus, shortcuts, and tool layouts to mirror Photoshop's interface, while adding default resources like fonts and brushes. This makes GIMP immediately usable for Photoshop veterans without retraining. You can apply it by copying the patch files into your GIMP configuration folder, instantly transforming the UI. It's ideal for designers, educators, or studios transitioning to free software.",
        "zh": "PhotoGIMP 是针对 GIMP 3+ 的补丁，旨在帮助 Photoshop 用户无缝迁移至开源图像编辑工具。它通过重新排列菜单、快捷键和工具布局模拟 Photoshop 界面，并预装常用字体与笔刷，显著降低学习成本。技术核心在于修改 GIMP 配置文件，无需编译源码即可一键应用。用户只需将补丁文件复制至配置目录并重启，即可获得熟悉操作体验。适合希望摆脱商业软件依赖的设计师、教育机构或工作室，尤其便于团队批量部署。用户可基于此思路进一步自定义快捷键或菜单，打造专属工作流。",
        "es": "PhotoGIMP is a patch that adapts GIMP 3+ to feel like Adobe Photoshop, reducing the learning curve for Photoshop users migrating to open-source tools. It rearranges menus, shortcuts, and tool layouts to mirror Photoshop's interface, while adding default resources like fonts and brushes. This makes GIMP immediately usable for Photoshop veterans without retraining. You can apply it by copying the patch files into your GIMP configuration folder, instantly transforming the UI. It's ideal for designers, educators, or studios transitioning to free software.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "PhotoGIMP gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "PhotoGIMP is a patch that adapts GIMP 3+ to feel like Adobe Photoshop, reducing the learning curve for Photoshop users migrating to open-source tools. It rearranges menus, shortcuts, and tool layouts to mirror Photoshop's interface, while adding default resources like fonts and brushes. This makes GIMP immediately usable for Photoshop veterans without retraining. You can apply it by copying the patch files into your GIMP configuration folder, instantly transforming the UI. It's ideal for designers, educators, or studios transitioning to free software.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Diolinux/PhotoGIMP for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
